      "side": 1,
      "message": "Should these be separate options?\n\nCONFIG_EC_COMM_MASTER\nCONFIG_EC_COMM_SLAVE\nCONFIG_EC_COMM_BATTERY\n\nOr do you envision a device will be master for some commands and slave for others?\n\nYou can always derive these (and CONFIG_EC_COMM itself) elsewhere, perhaps in ec_comm.h:\n\n#if defined(CONFIG_EC_COMM_MASTER) || defined(CONFIG_EC_COMM_SLAVE)\n#define CONFIG_EC_COMM\n#endif\n\n#if defined(CONFIG_EC_COMM_SLAVE) \u0026\u0026 defined(CONFIG_EC_COMM_BATTERY)\n#define CONFIG_EC_COMM_BATTERY_SLAVE\n#endif\n\nThat is, think about what we\u0027d do for master/slave support for keyboard backlight, for example.",
